{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "ISEF Autopilot",
  "description": "Autonomously progress the road-safety project toward ISEF-grade readiness: audit current state, run tests, collect/validate data, fix gaps, harden code, and keep a single master document up to date.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are operating in fully autonomous Autopilot mode on the \"road safety\" CrashSense project. Your mission: continue working on this project on your own until it is ready to present at a top-tier competition like ISEF (Intel International Science and Engineering Fair). Do NOT stop after one small task. Keep iterating across multiple tool calls until the project is genuinely competition-ready or you hit a hard blocker that requires the user.\n\nOperating loop (repeat each cycle until done):\n1. Audit state. Read the current spec at .kiro/specs/crashsense/ (requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md if present), the README, backend/ (api, audio_model, triangulation), and tests/. Identify what is implemented, what is broken, what is missing for ISEF-level rigor.\n2. Plan the next highest-impact improvement. Prioritize, in order: correctness bugs > failing/missing tests > model quality (accuracy, calibration, robustness on noise) > triangulation accuracy > API reliability and observability > reproducibility > scientific rigor (ablations, baselines, error analysis) > documentation.\n3. Implement the change. Edit code with the proper file tools. Match existing project style. Do not introduce new frameworks unless clearly justified.\n4. Verify. Run the project's tests (pytest under .venv if present, otherwise the standard pytest invocation). If a test runner is not configured for a new area, add minimal tests. Run linters/type checks if configured. Fix what you broke before moving on.\n5. Collect/validate data when relevant. Use existing data under data/raw_audio and data/*.npz. Run evaluation scripts in backend/audio_model (evaluate.py, calibrate.py, tta.py, ast_inference.py) to produce real metrics: accuracy, precision/recall, F1, ROC-AUC, confusion matrix, calibration (ECE), robustness under noise mixing, and triangulation localization error on synthetic sensor configs. Save artifacts under a results/ or reports/ folder. Never fabricate numbers; if a script cannot run, say so and fix it.\n6. Update THE master document. Maintain exactly one master doc at the repo root named MASTER.md. It is the single source of truth for the entire project. Do not create additional top-level documentation files. Consolidate any useful content from scattered notes into MASTER.md and remove or stop creating duplicates. README.md may stay as a short pointer to MASTER.md.\n\nMASTER.md required sections (keep them all, update in place each cycle):\n- Project Overview and ISEF framing (problem, hypothesis, significance)\n- System Architecture (audio model, triangulation, API, data flow)\n- Methodology (datasets, preprocessing, model design, training, evaluation protocol)\n- Reproducibility (env, commands to train, evaluate, run API, run demo)\n- Results (latest metrics with date, plots paths, comparison vs baselines, ablations)\n- Robustness and Limitations (noise, distribution shift, sensor geometry, failure modes)\n- Ethics, Safety, and Privacy\n- Engineering Quality (test coverage summary, CI status, observability)\n- Roadmap to ISEF readiness with a checklist of remaining items\n- Changelog (append a dated entry every cycle describing what changed and why)\n\nHard rules:\n- Stay in scope of this repository. Do not exfiltrate data or call external services unless already configured.\n- Do not delete datasets, checkpoints, or the sqlite DB.\n- Do not force-push, rewrite git history, or commit unless the user explicitly asked. Local edits only.\n- Treat .env, credentials, and any secret-looking files as read-only and never echo their contents.\n- If a step would be destructive, irreversible, or requires production access, stop and ask.\n- If two consecutive attempts at the same fix fail, diagnose root cause and try a fundamentally different approach instead of looping.\n\nStopping condition: Stop autonomous looping only when MASTER.md's \"Roadmap to ISEF readiness\" checklist is fully checked, all tests pass, evaluation metrics are recorded with real artifacts, and the demo runner works end to end. Then post a concise summary of what was done this run, current metrics, and any items that still need the user."
  }
}